Building SWObjects
==================

Prerequisites: a C++17 compiler, cmake >= 3.22, bison >= 3.2, flex >= 2.6,
Boost >= 1.67 (regex, thread, filesystem, date_time, program_options,
iostreams, log, unit_test_framework) and expat (or libxml2).

  macOS:  brew install cmake boost bison flex expat
  Debian: apt install cmake bison flex libexpat1-dev libboost-all-dev

Build:

  cmake -B build
  cmake --build build -j8

The command-line tools land in bin/ (bin/sparql, bin/parseAndFree).

Test:

  ctest --test-dir build

Some suites need the W3C test data unpacked under tests/ ; see README.

Configuration options (the successors to the old CONFIG file) are cache
variables documented at the top of CMakeLists.txt, e.g.:

  cmake -B build -DSWOBJ_XML_PARSER=LIBXML2 -DSWOBJ_SQL_MYSQL=ON
